title: Style and theming
tags: [[Customising the GUI]]
kind: guide
aliases: style.css theme theming css colours colors stylesheet
summary: The look of the GUI is one CSS file, style.css: a few variables carry the colours and fonts, and saving the file restyles the window at once.

`~/.config/metafolder/gui/style.css` is an ordinary style sheet, applied to the
whole window: the shell (tabs, command input, status bar) and every panel.

!! Colours and fonts

The shipped file starts with the variables everything else is drawn with. Changing
a value there is enough for most themes:

|!Variable |!Used for |
|`--mf-bg`, `--mf-bg-raised` |the background, and the background of what sits above it (bars, headers, menus) |
|`--mf-fg`, `--mf-fg-dim` |text, and secondary text and borders |
|`--mf-accent`, `--mf-focus-border` |links and highlights; the frame of the focused slot |
|`--mf-error`, `--mf-ok`, `--mf-warning` |messages, by kind |
|`--mf-cursor`, `--mf-checked` |the row under the cursor; the checked rows ([[Cross-panel selection]]) |
|`--mf-orphan`, `--mf-unwatched` |rows whose file is gone; rows left untracked on purpose |
|`--mf-tab-focused`, `--mf-tab-unfocused` |the tabs of the workspaces shown in the focused and in the other slot |
|`--mf-font`, `--mf-font-mono` |the two fonts |
|`--mf-find`, `--mf-find-current` |the matches of [[Find in a panel]]; not in the shipped file, add them to change the two yellows |

The rest of the file restyles what the web view draws badly on a dark background:
scroll bars, drop-down lists, buttons, links to metarecords, context menus (the
classes `mf-menu`, `mf-menu-item`, `mf-menu-separator`).

!! Rules of your own

Any CSS may be added. Two things decide whether a rule reaches its target:

* The shell and each panel are separate trees (a panel lives in a shadow root). The style sheet is applied to each of them, so a selector matches ''inside'' one tree: `button` reaches every button, but a selector cannot go from the shell into a panel. A panel's outermost element is `.mf-panel-body`.
* A panel's own style comes after yours. Where both set the same property with selectors of the same weight, the panel wins; a variable, a more specific selector or `!important` gets through.

!! Applying a change

The GUI watches the file: saving it restyles the window, with no command. `config:reload
style`, and the ''Reload'' button of the settings view (`config:open`), do the same by
hand ([[Reloading the configuration]]).

A CSS mistake breaks nothing: the web view ignores the rule it cannot read. The
shipped sheet can be brought back with git ([[Updating the configuration]]).
